{"kind":"table","sheet":"Curriculum","address":"A1:M3","rows":3,"cols":13,"values":[["Chapter","Topic","Concept","Prerequisite 1","Prerequisite 2","Prerequisite 3","Prerequisite 4","Prerequisite 5","Learning outcome 1","Learning outcome 2","Learning outcome 3","Learning outcome 4","Learning outcome 5"],["Vectors In Two Dimensions","Resultant of Perpendicular Vectors","Determining the Magnitude of the Resultant Using Theorem of Pythagoras","Be able to identify the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle.","Be able to use Pythagoras' theorem to find one side when the other two are known.","Be able to square a number and calculate a square root.","Be able to identify perpendicular directions in a diagram.","","Can you identify the right-angled triangle formed by perpendicular components and their resultant?","Can you calculate R = sqrt(R_x^2 + R_y^2)?","Can you give the magnitude as a non-negative value with the correct unit?","",""],["Vectors In Two Dimensions","Resultant of Perpendicular Vectors","Determining the Direction of the Resultant Using Simple Trigonometric Ratio","Be able to identify the opposite, adjacent and hypotenuse sides relative to an angle in a right-angled triangle.","Be able to use tan(theta) = opposite / adjacent.","Be able to use inverse tangent on a calculator in degree mode.","Be able to identify the four quadrants and the signs of x- and y-components.","","Can you calculate a reference angle from two non-zero perpendicular components?","Can you use the component signs to place the resultant in the correct quadrant?","Can you state its direction relative to a named axis or compass direction?","Can you identify the direction directly when one component is zero?",""]]}
